  "claimBoundary": "This is a strict source-bound zero-result conditional plan for testing Raspberry Pi Camera Module 3 Wide as a Pi-only CSI fallback after one exact shared-UVC product gate fails. D-043 keeps one replaceable wide-angle UVC camera as the cross-tier incumbent. The current source note that Camera Module 3 Wide has autofocus and a 120-degree diagonal field of view is merchandise capability context, not received-device, calibrated useful-area, image-quality, latency, enclosure, privacy, service, maintenance, or qualification evidence. Advertised field of view, a libcamera preview, one frame, lower glass-to-memory latency, cable convenience, a UVC driver fault, another camera, another target, an average, or an aggregate cannot open the fallback or prove that CSI materially closes the exact failure. Camera Module 3 Wide changes sensor, optics, lens, controls, rolling-shutter behavior and interface together, so its result is a complete camera-path comparison and cannot be attributed to CSI alone without a reviewed matched-hardware control. A failed UVC cell remains failed and CSI cannot qualify UVC, Steam Machine, ordinary x86 Linux, or the shared-camera product claim. Exact trigger evidence, cameras, revisions, lenses, drivers, modes, timestamps, target, enclosure, thresholds, schedule, results and authority remain open. No purchase, vendor contact, installation, ribbon routing, camera operation, participant collection, persistent calibration write, product selection, D-043 supersession, BOM mutation, publication, or compatibility claim is authorized.",
